---
title: Scallops, Asparagus, and Bacon Stir Fry
servings: 4
course: Main
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

Heat a #large frying pan or wok{} over a high heat and add a little of the @butter{25%g}. Sear the @scallops{8%large} for a minute or two on each side until just barely cooked through. Remove to a plate.

Add the @bacon{80%g}(cut into lardons) to the pan and fry until lightly browned, then remove and add to the scallops.

Add the @onion{0.5}(finely sliced) and remaining butter. Toss the onion for a minute until softened, then add the @asparagus{1%bunch}(cut into 5 cm lengths) and toss for about two minutes until the asparagus is just cooked. Add the @apple cider vinegar{} and season generously with @black pepper{} and a touch of @salt, if needed.

Return the bacon and scallops to the pan and toss to combine, then remove to a plate and serve with bread to mop up the buttery juices.